/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  chemistry/Glyc-formation.dat -- the first dissociation of glycolic acid, written from the master:
      HGlyc  <=>  Glyc + H+
  Made by bin/curate/species_c373.py from data/curation/batches/species_c373/*.tsv.

  logK25 and dH are the PRINTED values of the sources below (standard state ideal solution at 1 mol/kg, 298.15 K):
      pK1 = 3.831, dH1 = 0.46 kJ/mol
  Source: Miller & Smith-Magowan, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 19 (1990) 1049; H+(aq) = 0, zero ionic strength, aqueous species at 1 mol/dm3 (Table 1 caption, p. 1052).
  This record carries the first step (the sign flips with the direction written).
  The constant-dCp term of the printed dCp is NOT carried: the record grammar has no place for it (a
  van't Hoff integral with a constant dCp is exactly the `analytic` A1, A3, A4 terms; proposed, not done).
  Glycolic acid is not in Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen (2002); Miller & Smith-Magowan take its pK and dH_ion from Christensen & Hansen (their ref. 77CHR/HAN).
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType aqueousSpeciation;
schemaVersion 1;

species Glyc; masters ( { ion HGlyc; nu 1; } { ion H; nu -1; } );
      logK25 -3.831; dH 460; source "Miller & Smith-Magowan, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 19 (1990) 1049 -- Table 6, p. 1057: pK1 3.831, dH1 0.46 kJ/mol (read from a page image) (pK, dH_ion at 298.15 K)";
